l investigation</article-title><source>Med Educ</source><year>2001</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1034</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11703639</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2923.2001.01044.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McManus</surname><given-names>IC</given-names></name><name><surname>Keeling</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Paice</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress, burnout and doctors' attitudes to work are determined by personality and learning style: a twelve year longitudinal study of UK medical graduates</article-title><source>BMC Medicine</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>29</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15317650</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1741-7015-2-29</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shaufeli</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Enzmann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>The burnout companion to study and practice &#x02013; a critical analysis</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>London: Taylor and Francis</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hallsten L</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Torg&#x000e9;n</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>Performance-based self-esteem. A driving force in burnout processes and its assessment</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Stockholm: National Institute for Working Life</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahlin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Joneborg